{
  "title": "Classify closing the human GUI as an intentional session stop",
  "description": "The Windows subscription supervisor currently raises RuntimeError when the human GUI exits during play and records gameplay_harness_failure. Closing the window is an expected interactive stop action. Reproduce by starting windows/Play-vs-ChatGPT.cmd and closing the game window before a terminal game result. Cleanup works, but the manifest should distinguish user_closed_window/stopped from protocol failure and normal gameplay loss. Add a supervisor test with fake process states; no model inference should be needed.",
